# Grok 5 — negative findings by GLM 5.3 Flash

- Source: xAI (`grok-5` — announced, in training; NOT released as of 2026-11-04)
- Date: 2026-11-04 (UTC)
- Overview and scoring methodology: `../../model-comparison.md`
- Cross-model signed log: `../../model-findings.md`

## Model card

- **Name:** Grok 5
- **Short description:** xAI's announced next flagship model. Confirmed in training in xAI's January 2026 funding announcement and repeatedly teased by Elon Musk (6–10T-parameter rumors, native multimodality, "10% chance of AGI"). It has NOT shipped: as of early November 2026 there is no model card, no API identifier, no pricing, no launch post, and no official benchmark. xAI's current flagship is Grok 4.7 (released 2026-09-21, $2/$6 per 1M, 500K context).
- **Provider / access:** none — not available via API or consumer apps. docs.x.ai model list (fetched 2026-10-13 by the ZBuild tracker) shows `grok-4.7` and no `grok-5` entry. Musk's September 14, 2026 roadmap places Grok 4.8 and Grok 4.9 ahead of Grok 5, with no date; the last public window is "before end of 2026" (Musk, August 2026).
- **Release / knowledge:** unreleased. Timeline slipped repeatedly: "before end of 2025" → Q1 2026 → mid-2026 → 4.8/4.9 first → "before year-end 2026" (undated). An xAI preview of Grok 5 (memory/reasoning-speed claims) was given 2026-10-14 with no release date.
- **IDs:** none. No `grok-5` API model ID exists.
- **Context window:** no official figure. Rumors/estimates range 1.5M–2M; the shipped Grok 4.7 is 500K, Grok 4.3 is 1M. Unverified.
- **Modalities:** unverified. Native multimodality (text/image/voice/video) is "expected" per commentary but specified by no one at xAI.
- **Pricing:** unannounced.
- **Architecture:** unconfirmed. Parameter counts circulating (1.5T "V9-Medium" per a Musk X post; 6T–15T in various leaks) are explicitly unattributed rumor — no primary xAI document states any Grok 5 parameter count.

### Raw benchmarks found

> SELF-EXCLUSION: zero verified public benchmark numbers exist for a released Grok 5. The only numbers ever attached to the name are May 2026 pre-announcement claims (GPQA Diamond 89% / 94% "Heavy", HLE 18%, AIME 2026 96%, SWE-bench Verified 78%, vs GPT-5.5) from a Musk X post — never substantiated by a shipped model, an official model card, or independent reproduction, and contradicting xAI's own catalog (which still tops out at 4.7). Several trackers explicitly state "no official Grok 5 benchmark results have been released." Saved as `.md.excluded` per template rule — not scored.

Agent / tool use:

- Terminal-Bench (any version): no verified public score found (Grok 4.7 measured 37.6% on TB 4.0 — different model)
- OSWorld / GDPval-AA / Tau-family: no verified public score found

Reasoning / knowledge:

- GPQA Diamond / HLE / AIME: only the unverified May 2026 pre-announcement claims listed above; no independent or post-release verification

Coding:

- SWE-bench Verified: only the unverified 78% pre-announcement claim; no shipped-model score

Long context:

- no long-context retrieval reported

### Normalized scores (1–100)

Not scored — the model does not exist as a shipping product; every benchmark row is an unverified pre-announcement claim (self-exclusion rule). Conflict note: one review site lists Grok 5 as "Released 2026-06-02" and another as an X-Premium-bundled June ship; both are contradicted by the primary record (docs.x.ai model list lacking `grok-5` through at least 2026-10-13, xAI's news index listing no Grok 5 release through 2026-10-21, and Musk's 2026-09-14 roadmap putting 4.8/4.9 first). Primary record wins.

